-- Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA), 07-a0-00, Part VI: the two provisions the in-scope provisions
-- rely on without citing them, encoded as boundary modules at depth 1 (reference register REF-77, REF-82):
--   s 82 (contracting out), with r 7F; and
--   s 85 (service), with rr 7FA and 12I, which fixes the day every in-scope notice is given.
-- Source: sources/rta-1987.07-a0-00.mrdoc_49316.txt lines 2285-2292 (s 82) and 2301-2316 (s 85).
-- LQA step 4A, 4 October 2026. Not yet through 6H.

IMPORT `part-1-definitions`
IMPORT `regulations-1989`

§ `Section 82 -- Contracting out`

-- A term of an agreement, or an arrangement, and what is known about it. Whether a term is
-- inconsistent with a provision, or purports to restrict the Act, is decided by the provision it
-- touches; the cases supply the answer for the provision they test.
--   `provided for under the Act`: "Except as provided under this Act", e.g. s 30(2)(b), under which
--     the right to increase rent "may be excluded or limited by agreement".
DECLARE `Term or arrangement` HAS
    `inconsistent with a provision of the Act`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `purports to exclude, modify or restrict the operation of the Act`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `provided for under the Act`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a purported waiver of a right conferred by or under the Act`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `entered into with intent to defeat, evade or prevent the operation of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 82(1)(a); Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 7F
GIVEN t IS A `Term or arrangement`, a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(1)(a) -- the term is void` t `in` a IF
        NOT `r 7F -- section 82 does not apply to` a
    AND "Except as provided under this Act" ... NOT t's `provided for under the Act`
    AND (   "inconsistent with a provision of this Act" ... t's `inconsistent with a provision of the Act`
         OR "purports to exclude, modify or restrict the operation of this Act" ... t's `purports to exclude, modify or restrict the operation of the Act`)

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 82(1)(b); Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 7F
GIVEN t IS A `Term or arrangement`, a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(1)(b) -- the waiver is void` t `in` a IF
        NOT `r 7F -- section 82 does not apply to` a
    AND NOT t's `provided for under the Act`
    AND "any purported waiver of a right conferred by or under this Act" ... t's `a purported waiver of a right conferred by or under the Act`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 82(2); Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) r 7F
GIVEN t IS A `Term or arrangement`, a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82(2) -- entering into it is an offence` t `in` a IF
        NOT `r 7F -- section 82 does not apply to` a
    AND "with intent either directly or indirectly to defeat, evade or prevent the operation of this Act"
    ... t's `entered into with intent to defeat, evade or prevent the operation of the Act`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 82(2), Penalty
`s 82(2) -- the maximum fine` MEANS 10000

§ `Section 85 -- Service`

-- s 85(1)(a), (b), (c), (2), (4) with r 7FA (s 85(1)(ba)) and r 12I: the day on which a notice is
-- given, if the way it was given is one s 85 provides for.
-- (1)(a) personally: the day it is handed over.
-- (1)(b), (2) by post: "deemed to be effected at the time when the letter would have been delivered in
--   the ordinary course of post" (that day is a fact, REF-77).
-- (1)(c) electronically: "with the consent of that person or in other prescribed circumstances ... by
--   prescribed electronic means"; r 12I prescribes email only for an authorised notice. FK-12,
--   reading taken (A): an in-scope notice sent by email is not given under s 85(1)(c), consent or not.
--   The Act fixes no time at which an electronic notice is given; the encoding takes the day it is sent.
-- (1)(ba) [r 7FA]: left at the premises by the Housing Authority as lessor.
-- (4)(a), (b): given to a person apparently over 16 apparently residing at the premises, or to the
--   person who ordinarily pays the rent: deemed duly given to the tenant.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 85(1), (2), (4); Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) rr 7FA, 12I; fork FK-12 reading A
GIVEN g IS A `Giving of a notice`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 85 -- the day the notice is given` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g's `way`
    WHEN `personally (s 85(1)(a))` THEN JUST (g's `on`)
    WHEN `by post (s 85(1)(b))` THEN JUST (g's `day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`)
    WHEN `by email (s 85(1)(c))` THEN
        IF     (   g's `the recipient consented to electronic service`
                OR `r 12I(2)(a) -- prescribed circumstances exist for` g)
           AND `r 12I(2)(b) -- email is a prescribed electronic means for` g
        THEN JUST (g's `on`)
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `left at the premises by the Housing Authority (r 7FA)` THEN
        IF `r 7FA -- s 85(1)(ba) -- the notice may be left at the premises` g THEN JUST (g's `on`) ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `to a person apparently over 16 apparently residing at the premises (s 85(4)(a))` THEN JUST (g's `on`)
    WHEN `to the person who ordinarily pays the rent (s 85(4)(b))` THEN JUST (g's `on`)

-- FK-12, reading rejected (B): a notice sent by email to a person who consented to electronic service
-- is given on the day it is sent, whatever its kind.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 85(1)(c); fork FK-12 reading B
GIVEN g IS A `Giving of a notice`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`FK-12 reading B -- s 85 -- the day the notice is given` g MEANS
    IF     g's `way` EQUALS `by email (s 85(1)(c))`
       AND g's `the recipient consented to electronic service`
    THEN JUST (g's `on`)
    ELSE `s 85 -- the day the notice is given` g

-- s 85(3): a notice that cannot be given under subsection (1) is deemed given if published in a
-- daily newspaper circulating in the State, given by a court-ordered alternative means, or made
-- publicly available in a prescribed manner (r 12 prescribes one only for court notices under s 18(2)).
DECLARE `Substituted giving` HAS
    `the notice cannot be given under s 85(1)`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copy published in a daily newspaper circulating in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a court-ordered alternative means effected`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `made publicly available in a prescribed manner`              IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 85(3)
GIVEN x IS A `Substituted giving`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 85(3) -- the notice is deemed to have been given` x IF
        x's `the notice cannot be given under s 85(1)`
    AND (   "(a)" ... x's `a copy published in a daily newspaper circulating in the State`
         OR "(b)" ... x's `a court-ordered alternative means effected`
         OR "(c)" ... x's `made publicly available in a prescribed manner`)

-- s 85(5): a notice to a lessor is deemed duly given if given to the property manager, to a person
-- apparently over 16 apparently residing at the lessor's place of residence, or to the person who
-- ordinarily receives the rent.
DECLARE `Person a notice to the lessor is given to` IS ONE OF
    `the lessor`
    `the property manager of the premises`
    `a person apparently over 16 apparently residing at the lessor's place of residence`
    `the person who ordinarily receives the rent`
    `someone else`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 85(5)
GIVEN p IS A `Person a notice to the lessor is given to`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 85(5) -- the notice is duly given to the lessor, given to` p IF
    NOT (p EQUALS `someone else`)

-- s 85(6): where there are 2 or more lessors or tenants, giving the notice to any one of them is
-- sufficient compliance.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 85(6)
GIVEN recipients IS A LIST OF STRING
      parties    IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 85(6) -- a notice given to` recipients `is given to the lessors or tenants` parties IF
    `some member of` recipients `is among` parties
